{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And you.</b> I have already said that every priest is always a minister, and the proof is \"our Elohim's ministers.\" So the nations will be counterpart to Israel, and Israel counterpart to the sons of Aaron; therefore, the wealth of the nations corresponds to the tithe." "The yod in תתימרו is in place of the alef, from the same root as את יי האמרת (Deuteronomy 26:17)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 61, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra's Hebrew explicitly specifies 'yod in place of alef' as letters; his Hebrew citation of the root form is rendered verbatim."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:37.333362266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}